   "text": {
    "L1": "Germination is when a seed starts growing into a young plant, or sprout.",
    "L2": "A seed needs water, air and suitable warmth to germinate.",
    "L3": "It does not need soil or sunlight yet, because food is stored inside the seed.",
    "L4": "That is why moong can sprout on wet cotton, even in the dark.",
    "L5": "But seeds kept fully under water get too little air and germinate poorly or not at all.",
    "L6": "To test one condition fairly, change only that condition and keep the rest the same.",
    "L7": "For air, use wet cotton in an open glass and seeds fully under water in another glass.",
    "L8": "Keep the same seeds, number, place and time, then compare the sprouts after four days."
   },
